<title>USA: Chrysler 1996 U.S. sales exceed 2.4 mln units.</title>
<headline>Chrysler 1996 U.S. sales exceed 2.4 mln units.</headline>
<dateline>AUBURN HILLS, Mich. 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Corp said Thursday its U.S. sales total for calendar-year 1996 exceeded 2.4 million vehicles, setting a new company record.</p>
<p>Chrysler said the previous high was 2,208,057 vehicles in 1988.</p>
<p>The automaker is scheduled to release its complete U.S. sales statistics at about 1000 EST on Friday. Through November, Chrysler's U.S. sales have been running about 14 percent ahead of a year ago.</p>
</text>
